  "meta-title": "Post Webinar Survey Builder and Question Guide | Emergent",
  "meta-description": "Create a post webinar survey with the right questions, open it from any webinar tool, and send demo requests to your CRM. Free to start.",
  "name": "Build a Post Webinar Survey That Shapes Your Next Session",
  "acrm---product-name": "Post Webinar Survey Builder",
  "description": "Build a post webinar survey attendees open as the session ends, with demo requests sent to your CRM and every answer saved.",
  "acrm---breadcrumb": "Post Webinar Survey",
  "explore-cta": "Build My Post Webinar Survey",
  "awb---how-to-title": "How to Create a Post Webinar Survey",
  "awb---how-to-description": "Seven steps to plan a post webinar survey, build it with Emergent, and act on what attendees tell you.",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Post Webinar Survey FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are some good questions to include in a post-webinar survey?\", \"a\": \"Open on how attendees rate the session overall, from 1 to 5, and what they found most useful. Then ask what was still unclear, how each speaker did, and which topic they want covered next. Finish on the step the webinar was meant to drive, such as a demo request. Write each of these post-webinar survey questions about the session you ran, not about webinars in general.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a post webinar survey?\", \"a\": \"Describe the webinar, its audience, and the questions you want in a plain-English prompt, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> turns it into a working survey with a results dashboard and a database behind it. Publish it, put the link on your closing slide and in the replay email, and edit any question later with one more prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a post-webinar survey template enough, or should each session get its own?\", \"a\": \"A post-webinar survey template is a fine start for the rating and comment questions, which stay the same every time. Write the rest for the session: name the topic in the usefulness question and match the closing question to the webinar's goal. With Emergent, you describe those changes in a prompt and the survey is rebuilt to match.\"}, {\"q\": \"How is a post-webinar survey different from one for an in-person event?\", \"a\": \"It asks about the stream itself: whether the audio and video played without breaking up, and whether attendees stayed to the end. It leaves out the venue and catering questions that a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/post-event'>post event survey</a> covers.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the best time to show a post-webinar survey to attendees?\", \"a\": \"Show it the moment the session ends, then send it again with the replay. A Zoom webinar host can schedule a survey to be sent to attendees and panelists when the webinar ends, and can redirect them to a third-party survey service instead. Close the survey after about a week, while attendees still remember the session.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a post-webinar survey have?\", \"a\": \"Keep it to 8 questions or fewer for an hour-long webinar, and about 5 for a 30-minute one. Put the rating first and the demo question last, since those two feed the next decision. Anything past that limit can go in a follow-up survey to the people who asked to hear more.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I run a post-webinar survey after an online class or a livestreamed service?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The core questions carry over: rate the session and say what was still unclear. For a livestreamed service, ask about the stream itself, such as sound and video, and leave questions about congregation life to a separate <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/church'>church survey</a>. Emergent builds either one from a prompt, with no response cap.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a post-webinar survey be anonymous?\", \"a\": \"Keep the ratings anonymous and the contact details optional. People rate a session more freely when their name is not attached, but a demo request is useless without a name and email. Ask for contact details only in the question where someone asks for a next step, and say so in that question.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I get more attendees to answer a post-webinar survey?\", \"a\": \"Ask while they are still in the session. Mention the survey before the last audience question, show the link as a QR code on the last slide, and make the first question a single tap. Send one reminder with the replay link and stop there. Each response is saved to a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a post-webinar survey sign people up for a next step like volunteering?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Add a yes-or-no question for the next step and have the app add each yes to a sign-up list with the person's name and email. To collect availability and preferred shifts, send a separate <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/volunteer'>volunteer survey</a> to the people who said yes instead of lengthening the webinar survey.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "alpb---prompt": "<p>Build a post webinar survey that collects every answer in a database I own.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a post webinar survey that collects every answer in a database I own.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Demo Requests\", \"add\": \"Add demo requests that send each attendee who asks for a demo to HubSpot.\"}, {\"label\": \"Session Ratings\", \"add\": \"Add session ratings on a 1-5 scale and average them on the dashboard.\"}, {\"label\": \"Phone Layout\", \"add\": \"Add a phone layout that shows one question per screen.\"}, {\"label\": \"Speaker Feedback\", \"add\": \"Add speaker feedback questions that rate each presenter.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
